// Drift guard (spec §5.6): every typed knob's code default must equal the value shipped in
// the legacy conf/ tree. Reads the repository's conf/ files directly, so a change to either
// side without the other fails here instead of silently diverging again.
//
// Battle knobs: BattleConfig holds every entry of legacy battle_data[] (src/map/battle.cpp),
// partly hand-typed and partly generated by tools/codegen/battle_knobs.py. The "shipped"
// default the reimagined server uses is the conf/battle value, because that is what an operator
// running the legacy server gets; the legacy code default only matters for knobs that no conf
// file sets. Where the legacy code default and the shipped conf disagree, the difference is
// listed below on purpose (kKnownCodeVsConfDifferences) so that a new one fails the test.
#include <gtest/gtest.h>

